--- Finding (json): a parsed JSON whole number outside a signed 64-bit int
--- (above 2^63 - 1, or below -2^63) is read through a float: int[] of it
--- answers another number, type[] says float, and the number past 64 bits
--- is held as a float from the parse (encode writes 1.2345678901234568e+29).
--- The same in both modes:
---   float
---   18446744073709551616
---   123456789012345677877719597056
---   [9007199254740993,18446744073709551615,1.2345678901234568e+29]
---   runtime error: line 25: a parsed value holds a number 18446744073709551615
---   where the program reads a number (met in add at line 25): a float holds a
---   whole number exactly only up to 2^53 — int[…] reads it as it is
--- Expected (spec, JSON: "A parsed whole number is held as it is: … encode
--- writes it with every digit, and int[…] reads it exactly"; an int is a whole
--- number of any size): int, 18446744073709551615,
--- 123456789012345678901234567890, and encode writing every digit. The stop's
--- own advice, "int[…] reads it as it is", answers …616 for …615. Within
--- signed 64 bits (9007199254740993) it is right. -9223372036854775809 gives
--- -9223372036854775808 alike.
d = json['[9007199254740993, 18446744073709551615, 123456789012345678901234567890]']
log[type[d[1]]]
log[int[d[1]]]
log[int[d[2]]]
log[encode[d]]
log[d[1] + 1]
